    "source_text": "Anadimos \"a\" pq es muy muy especifico"
  },
  {
    "id": "row501",
    "rows": [
      501
    ],
    "category": "vocab_spanish_only",
    "source_text": "In this section of the text, el tiempo is the subject here, that's why I was confused, like I was like who is the subject/narrator/central person, bc who is that person or point of reference who is telling us that on the left is that girl and on the right is the other?"
  },
  {
    "id": "row503",
    "rows": [
      503
    ],
    "category": "vocab_spanish_only",
    "source_text": "So in my last sentence I was talking about this, and Marcia was confused I only wrote \"cambiando\" and not \"intercambiando\", even though in the original text was also \"cambiar\", but apparently there it was clear bc of context prior."
  },
  {
    "id": "row505",
    "rows": [
      505
    ],
    "category": "vocab_spanish_only",
    "source_text": "So she told me to read story again with \"el tiempo\" as subject/narrator. And yes, it's weird that the \"time\" is like apparently looking at the rearview mirror, and all these other actions (infitinitivo verbs), but well, it's a realism fantasy style/epoca, so things don't make literal sense.."
